        {
          "id": "2726ba1c-0f30-35e0-beb1-2efdd151d5c5",
          "content": {
            "id": "2726ba1c-0f30-35e0-beb1-2efdd151d5c5",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Dayforce shareholders back Thoma Bravo's $12.3 billion take-private deal",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "The preliminary results of a special meeting held on Wednesday showed that about 88.4% of votes were in favor \u2060of the Thoma \u200cBravo deal.  The software sector has emerged as an investment target due to resilient subscription \u200dservices and recurring revenue in an economy weighed down by a deteriorating labor market, trade tariffs and erratic spending.  T. \u200bRowe Price Associates, with a 15.7% \u200cstake in Dayforce, had in October said it would vote against the transaction, calling the offer \"underwhelming\" and an attempt to take advantage of \"short-term pessimism\" in the sector.",
